[Music]  despite apparently covering up  new york's nursing home deaths at the  time governor andrew cuomo  will rake in more than five million  dollars for his book  praising what he did during the pandemic  janice dean lost both of her in-laws  after they developed covid19  in one of the state's long-term care  facilities  and in her op-ed in the new york post  this morning she says  the only place cuomo's book belongs is  under  the true crimes section fox news senior  meteorologist  janice dean joins us right now good  morning to you janice  good morning steve cover of the new york  post it's the big story  people are shocked that he would get  five  five million dollars uh to write this  book  where he talks about what a great job he  did but when you look at it  he didn't do such a good job your  in-laws are dead because of his decision  you  say listen when i first read that the  governor was writing a book in the  middle of the pandemic  i thought it was a joke i thought it was  a headline in the babylon b  or the onion how could the governor  write a book about leadership  when thousands of elderly were dying  it was incredible and i was mad at the  time  but seeing that he got over five million  dollars for this  profiting off the deaths of new yorkers  including my in-laws  it's disgusting and when you look at the  numbers  of according to publicly available  numbers it looks like he sold just  shy of 50 000 books and when you do the  math that means the governor himself  made about a hundred dollars per book  from his book advance when when you  do the math five million dollars fifty  thousand books  that's a deal i've never heard of  it's incredible but i think the book  publishing company can sue him for  breach of contract  because it's filled with lies and if you  look at the timeline  the governor covering up the nursing  home issue  the tragedy over fifteen thousand deaths  that  him and his administration tried to  cover up for months the timeline  corresponds with him trying to sell that  five million dollar book  so i wonder if we can profit off the son  of sam law  all of that money should go to the  families of our dead  loved ones well a lot of the money went  to his family his uh spokesperson put  out this  uh statement to fox news from that net  income the five million dollars  the governor donated a third to the  united way of new york state for  statewide coveted relief and vaccination  effort  for which i believe he did get a tax uh  you know a tax deduction and is given  the remainder  in a trust for his three daughters  equally who worked with the governor  during this pandemic  and did what he calls tireless and  effective work for all new yorkers  and gave him the strength and love to  make it through the crisis  every day but janice you know he would  not have  gotten that lucrative deal had the  actual numbers been out there and now  the more we see the more we realize  it sounds like behind the scenes they  were trying to keep the real numbers out  of the press  so he could get as big a deal as  possible  which he certainly did well i hope  ultimately this book is his downfall and  it's used against him in a court of law  because as i mentioned it's full of  lies so when he goes to court which i  hope he will in  all of the investigations against him i  hope that they use his leadership book  and throw it at him all right janice  dean you can read her op-ed  the pages of the new york post dot com  janice thank you

